DESCRIPTION:Bike lanes aren't just for bikes\; they’re mobility lanes. S
 afe\, connected infrastructure means access and independence for people of
  all abilities. Join Bike Brigade\, Cycle Toronto and the Kidical Mass TO 
 crew for the ACCESS FOR ALL ride on OCTOBER 31'st. Meetup at 10am at Chris
 tie Pits and rollout at 10:30am. We'll end the ride at Queen's Park with s
 peeches and and light snacks.\n\nDetails\n\n* Date: October 31\n* Time: 10
 :00 AM meet-up\, 10:30 AM roll out\n* Meeting Location: South East corner 
 of Christie Pits\n\n* * For more information regarding Christie subway sta
 tion and accessibility click (https://www.ttc.ca/subway-stations/christie-
 station) here.\n\n* Route: Bloor > St. George > Hoskin > Queen's Park (sub
 ject to change)\n\nIf you plan to meet us for the speeches at Queen's Park
 \, our designated meeting spot is highlighted by the red box below. For th
 ose taking wheel-trans\, please travel northbound on Queen’s Park Cresce
 nt East and turn left onto the south drive. Please consult the wheel-trans
  app ahead to time to plan your trip.\n\nCycle Toronto is proud to be powe
 ring the return of KidicalMassTO on the last Saturday of every month until
  October.\n\nKidical Mass is an international movement for child- and cycl
 ing-friendly cities. Kidical Mass rides are an all-ages\, all-abilities ce
 lebration of cycling that highlights the need for healthier cities. Kids a
 nd their grown-ups ride their bikes together.\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca
 /mobility_lanes
